# Scripted input for programs/conform-program (README "Conformance image"), the
# same as programs/conform's: conform.c built with -DPROGRAM checks the same events.
# conform.c checks these exact events (ev_want, t_pads), so keep the two in
# step.

# Frames 2-5: one of each kind of input event; the program reads the queue
# at frame 6 and compares it with ev_want.
2 down a shift ctrl
2 up a
2 press enter alt meta
3 text aé你😀
3 pointer 639 479 7
3 pointer 0 0 0
4 click 320 240
4 wheel -3 2
4 wheel 127 -127
5 feeds-updated
5 feeds-updated   # a second one in the same frame is dropped (SPEC §content.events)
5 down f12 meta
5 up 0xE7

# Frame 8: 70 text events; the queue holds 64 (SPEC §events), read at frame 9.
8 text 0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789

# Controllers (SPEC §controllers), read at frames 9 (none), 10, 11, 12 and 13.
10 pad 0 2013 -127 127 5 -5
10 pad 2 ffff 0 0
12 pad 0 1 0 0
13 pad 0 off
13 pad 2 off

# The page (conform.c t_page): in frame 140, presses over the big anchored
# text at the rectangle's top left, with the primary and then the secondary
# button (each gives a page-anchor event after its pointer event), over
# plain text and over no text (neither gives one); read at frame 141.
140 click 52 64
140 pointer 52 64 2
140 pointer 52 64 0
140 click 52 150
140 click 590 430

# The figure (conform.c t_page): a press over it in frame 143, read at 144.
143 click 590 130
